SUMMARY
The Valdorian Times has published another groundbreaking article ahead of the election. This time, it's about the incumbent mayoral candidate. According to the Times, the Mayor took bribes from FramtidX, a development company, to allow them to build a mall on protected land, a special marsh home to endangered frogs. Is this another fake story published by the Times, or is there any truth to it?

LEARNING OBJECTIVES
- Investigate website defacement and trace it to compromised credentials
- Identify internal spearphishing campaigns tailored to employee roles
- Recognize credential harvesting through fake login pages
- Trace file manipulation: deletion, download, and renaming
- Follow email collection, staging, and chunked exfiltration
- Understand hacktivist motivations versus financially-motivated attackers
- Map reconnaissance activity to target selection

